{{!-- The read-only tag row. One partial, three call sites: under the name on an item sheet,
      inline on an inventory slot line, and on an NPC's flat list — so an item reads the same in
      every place. `showEquipped` is off in the slot list, where equipment is already carried by
      the bold name and the lit hand control. `noSlotTags` is on for the NPC list: *petty* and
      *bulky* mean nothing without a slot count, and 2e binds no NPC to one. --}}
{{!-- A relic unknown to this user (`hidden`) prints no die and no armour: they are part of what
      its guise hides. Its slots are not — weight is something the holder feels. --}}
{{#unless hidden}}
{{#if system.blast}}<span class="cairn-item-tag">{{localize 'CAIRN.Blast'}}</span>{{/if}}
{{#if system.armor}}<span class="cairn-item-tag">{{localize 'CAIRN.Armor'}} {{system.armor}}</span>{{/if}}
{{#if system.damage}}<span class="cairn-item-tag">{{system.damageLabel}} {{localize 'CAIRN.Damage'}}</span>{{/if}}
{{/unless}}
{{!-- A sack says how much is in it; that number is its weight (`data/item-coin.js`), so it
      sits where the slot words sit, and a sack is never called bulky. --}}
{{#if system.isCoin}}<span class="cairn-item-tag">{{system.value}} {{localize 'CAIRN.GoldAbbrev'}}</span>{{/if}}
{{!-- Part of the body weighs nothing and is never put down, so the slot words and Equipped say
      nothing true of it; the one word that does is Body — except in the Body zone
      (`inBody`), where the place already says it. --}}
{{#if system.bodily}}{{#unless inBody}}<span class="cairn-item-tag">{{localize 'CAIRN.Body'}}</span>{{/unless}}{{else}}
{{#unless noSlotTags}}
{{#if system.bulky}}<span class="cairn-item-tag">{{localize 'CAIRN.Bulky'}}</span>{{/if}}
{{#if system.petty}}<span class="cairn-item-tag">{{localize 'CAIRN.Petty'}}</span>{{/if}}
{{/unless}}
{{#if showEquipped}}{{#if system.equipped}}<span class="cairn-item-tag">{{localize 'CAIRN.Equipped'}}</span>{{/if}}{{/if}}
{{/if}}
